      "side": 1,
      "message": "So noticed that if I use `--layering_check` on the command like everything gets checked and `cms` currently does not build that way in a component build. Added `features \u003d [\"layering_check\"],` to `tools/skdiff/BUILD.bazel` to enable the check just for skdiff. This gets the errors the g3 build is giving which is nice, but it does mean that I cannot use anything in `//src/base:base` because I don\u0027t have visibility.\n\nIn theory I suppose most of the stuff in `base` we don\u0027t want to export for anyone to just use for just whatever. However, it would be nice to have a component that our own tools can use. I note that `base` current allows `//tests:__subpackages__` so we could add `//tools:__subpackages__` to this list, I suppose?",
      "parentUuid": "73191bcb_d55ce6e0",
